  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` now passes with 6 tests (4 are new).\n\n- **Hang after a failed job:** a rejected job never decremented `running` or started the next job. A job that threw synchronously also broke the queue, and a plain return value crashed it because `.then` was called on a non-promise. Every job's outcome is now normalised to a promise, and `running` is decremented in every case.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving too early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also requires nothing running.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until `concurrency` slots are full.\n\nThe new tests in `test/queue.test.js` cover:\n- Async and sync failures not stopping the queue.\n- `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs.\n- `onIdle()` resolving immediately when the queue is already idle.\n- `resume()` filling all four slots with concurrency 4.\n\nI didn't check that the new tests fail on the old code.",
